ready: 1
kind: module
id: health
name: Health
summary: >-
  The memory's self-checks: one anxiety score with the actions that lower it, a
  doctor that checks the stack's integrity and setup, and metamemory that says
  how sure the agent can be of what it remembers. It reads every module's data
  and writes only through other modules' calls.
runs_in:
  - sys.python
  - sys.cli
  - sys.daemon
owns:
  - the anxiety score and its dimensions
  - integrity checks
  - confidence, uncertainty, gap and contradiction reports
invariants:
  - There is one anxiety calculation; the Python package, command line, tool server and status all report the same score for the same stack and moment.
  - Every reported problem names the call that resolves it.
  - Health reports never change memory content.
rationale: >-
  Health tells the agent and the owner what needs attention, not what Kernle
  could do for itself. Routine processing debt is handled by sleep, so the
  anxiety score counts only what the agent or owner must resolve: context
  about to be lost, unsaved work, decisions waiting in review, an incoherent
  identity, uncertain memory, and a stale epoch.
